Z||000000||redfiero||10-02-2001||06:34 AM||||Anyone know where the pilot light is for my car?  I can't get any fire.<P>Last week she plain died.  Accessories work but the engine won't run.  Over the weekend, I checked the fuses, changed the coils and crank position sensor, and still no fire.  I can hear the ECM firing the fuel pump when I turn the key.  Does this mean that my ECM is okay?  Anyone got any ideas of what it could be?  Anything that I can jumper out to troubleshoot the problem?  The computer is putting out no codes either.<P>I read Ogre's explanation on the DIS system.  If anyone has questions about the way that it works, I suggest reading the DIS Notes section.<P>Any suggestions are welcome!<P>Thanks,<BR>matt<BR>P.S. - 88 4 cyl.||||reg||11
Z||000001||Gerald||10-02-2001||10:36 AM||||this might be a kick in the pants but when that happened to my 87 it turned out being my timing gears. Had to drop the motor. Not fun. If its is the timing gears I suggust you get a new after market set.The stock set uses a kinda paper mache cam gear. That was my problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||10-02-2001||10:38 AM||||Try the magnetic pickup.  I've had them go bad.||||reg||1
